# Admin Settings Structure Rule

- Place every setting in its logical admin module only.
- Do not add random settings into unrelated sections.
- Keep related settings together under one dedicated area.
- Avoid duplicate setting screens for the same feature.
- Reuse existing modules before creating new settings pages.

## Required module placement

- Email templates: `Admin -> Email Templates`.
- Email event mapping/automation: `Admin -> Email Settings`.
- UI/theme controls: `System Management -> Theme & UI`.
- Trading account/group/leverage/platform controls: `System Management` dedicated sections.

## Change safety

- If a setting already exists, update it in place.
- If placement is unclear, use `System Management Dashboard` as the source of truth.
